For the interaction described in section 5.4.1 to take place a main rotor blade
trailing tip vortex must be cut by that part of a tail rotor blade that is outboard of the
point of maximum bound circulation. If the main rotor vortex is positioned such that it
will lie inboard of that point then a different interaction will occur. With the main rotor
vortex far enough inboard, its distance from the tail rotor trailing tip vortex should
result in there being insufficient strain on that vortex for disintegration to occur.
