5.7 Concluding remarks.
In Chapter 4, it was shown that study of the frequency content of the data
recorded on the Lynx AH Mk5 tail rotor had different attributes depending on aircraft
relative speed and direction. The low speed flight envelope of the aircraft was thus
divided into six regions. In this chapter, the effects noted in each of the six regions
were investigated in some depth and details on the interaction mechanisms taking place
revealed. Some of the mechanisms are clearly aircraft configuration related but it is
thought that others will be more universal in their application. Nearly all of the
mechanisms postulated warrant additional research, most of which would be best
carried out in a controlled wind tunnel environment.


